## Why This Is Asked
The question probes implementation of a real, scalable multi-tenant rate limiter using a kernel dataplane with live policy reloads. It tests practicality, correctness, and operability in a CNF gateway.

## Key Concepts
- eBPF maps and perf events
- Per-tenant scoping of policies
- Token bucket/rate-limiting with TTL
- Hot-reload of policy from ConfigMaps
- Domain pattern matching and testing in a single namespace

